  "observations": [
    "Final C-only list transport run 03 passes 225 rows/26 complete native images at actual 1x/2x, including actual older 528-byte-provider fallback. The independent ordinary list reference passes 108/26 and records native state/selected IDs and native scrollbar geometry as binary test data. Current radio wire regression passes 163/42. Combined scoped total is 496 rows/94 images; all 35 existing provider/transport regression sections pass separately.",
    "Native list replies match every independent native field: count/flags, primary/key/action uint64 IDs, every selected uint64 ID, document size and visible rectangle. Pointer/key/Shift actions, single/multiple selection, wheel/scrolling, empty data and disabled-row scrollbar behavior match native references. Owner-connection attacks cannot read/change/input/destroy another connection's list.",
    "Malformed models, invalid UTF8, bad item flags/reserved data, duplicate/zero IDs, unknown keys/flags, wrong row count/trailing bytes, multiple selection in single mode and wrong/nonfinite density are rejected without changing the previous native state. Read/draw remain available during original tracking while model/config/scroll mutation is refused. Late model messages cannot implicitly recreate destroyed controls.",
    "The first complete run passes 219/26. Run 02 additionally checks actual backing density in replies. Final run 03 adds explicit oversized initial-allocation cleanup and successful valid creation afterward, reaching 225/26. Earlier passing raw observations remain separate from the final scoped total.",
    "The C native-reference probe adds state/selection/scrollbar-geometry observations to its existing actual AppKit comparisons. Reference 01 predates scrollbar-geometry files; final reference 02 includes them. Its exact source snapshot is retained under .build/native-ui/list-wire-source-01; later protocol comments add density documentation without changing its state layout.",
    "This checkpoint rebuilds only small test probes. Runtime retains 20 production hashes, prior browser-adapter hashes, the unchanged provider/loader/shim and package count 1050. Current UI API readback is version 1/568, with no owned candidate mappings. Stderr notices are retained in runtime evidence."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Chromium and Gecko listbox/multiple-select bindings, original DOM focus/default/input/change/cancellation transactions, native intrinsic layout and option identity/lifetime handling.",
    "List model/selection/scroll replay through actual session-host replacement, pidfd owner cleanup and broader renderer lifecycle. Existing general cleanup is reused but this checkpoint does not qualify every list recovery scenario.",
    "Large payloads/lists beyond current bounded IPC, richer rows/group headers/separators, topology/visibility/transforms, mixed-DPI/browser zoom, accessibility/IME and native focus traversal.",
    "Remaining browser controls, complete detached menus/native shortcuts, derivatives and installed deployment; subsequent GTK/Qt/KDE integration through the same shared layer. Browser toolbar/address bar/tabs remain original; future requested changes use optional per-app patches."
  ],
